      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Alabama?",
      "a": "The state received $11.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Alabama had 81,432 awards at an average award size of $140K, and obligations fell 37.2% year over year. These totals are partial fiscal-year figures and represent contract obligations only."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Alabama?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts, obligating $8.1B in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the second largest buyer at $1.8B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $407M and the General Services Administration at $377M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Alabama?",
